{"id":2555,"date":"2021-03-19T14:11:12","date_gmt":"2021-03-19T14:11:12","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?post_type=student&#038;p=2555"},"modified":"2021-03-19T14:23:09","modified_gmt":"2021-03-19T14:23:09","slug":"seth-kurankyi-asante-2","status":"publish","type":"student","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/student\/seth-kurankyi-asante-2\/","title":{"rendered":"Seth Kurankyi Asante"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-background-dim profile-banner bg-alt\" style=\"background-color:none\"><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n\n\n<a href=\"javascript:history.back()\"> <div class=\"profiles-btn\"> \n\n<div class=\"btn-left-sq bg-primary\"> <i class=\"fa fa-caret-left white-text\"> <\/i> <\/div>\n<div class=\"btn-text title-bold white-text\">Back to Profiles<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/a>\n\n<h2 class=\"profile-name\">Seth Kurankyi Asante <\/h2>\n\n<p class=\"primary-bold profile-position prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>Ghana<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-info profile-tagline primary-bold prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>Class of 2013<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5 profile-body\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/Seth_photo1-1-2.jpeg\"\/>\n\n\n<p>Seth graduated with a degree in Mathematics, from the University of Ghana in 2011. He then proceeded to pursue a Masters in Mathematical Sciences, graduating from AIMS Ghana in 2013. He is currently a theoretical physicist working in the field of quantum gravity. As one of the few Africans in this field, he serves as a support system for African future researchers. He is also open to mentoring new students into the field. Having enough experts in theoretical physics across Africa will help to contribute to the development of science within the continent. Physics has proven to be at the heart of developing new forms of technology, in the modern world. His area of research tries to understand how gravity and quantum particles interact. Testing these theories require that new technologies are formed, which he believes will be useful and lead to the improvement of lives.<\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Seth graduated with a degree in Mathematics, from the University of Ghana in 2011. He then proceeded to pursue a Masters in Mathematical Sciences, graduating from AIMS Ghana in 2013. He is currently a theoretical physicist working in the field of quantum gravity. As one of the few Africans in this field, he serves as<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":10,"featured_media":2520,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"advgb_blocks_editor_width":"","advgb_blocks_columns_visual_guide":"","profile-testimonial":"","profile-success":"","profile-studentbio":"","profile-studentname":"Seth Kurankyi Asante ","profile-country":"Ghana","profile-program":"Class of 2013"},"tags":[],"student_types":[13],"acf":[],"featured_img":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/Seth_photo1-1-2.jpeg","coauthors":[],"author_meta":{"author_link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/author\/charlene\/","display_name":"charlene"},"relative_dates":{"created":"Posted 5 years ago","modified":"Updated 5 years ago"},"absolute_dates":{"created":"Posted on March 19, 2021","modified":"Updated on March 19, 2021"},"absolute_dates_time":{"created":"Posted on March 19, 2021 2:11 pm","modified":"Updated on March 19, 2021 2:23 pm"},"featured_img_caption":"","tax_additional":{"post_tag":{"linked":[],"unlinked":[],"slug":"post_tag","name":"Tags"},"student_types":{"linked":["<a href=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/student_type\/alumni\/\" class=\"advgb-post-tax-term\">Alumni<\/a>"],"unlinked":["<span class=\"advgb-post-tax-term\">Alumni<\/span>"],"slug":"student_types","name":"Student Type"}},"series_order":"","_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/s